{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And the Avvim who dwelt in Hazeroth as far as Azzah.</b> Even though they were descendants of Esav or of the Philistines to whom Avraham had sworn, Israel did not refrain from conquering their land. The reason for this was that Israel did not find the land in their [the Avvim's] possession — for the Caphtorim who went forth from Caphtor, due to the population pressure in the city from which they had gone out to seek a resting place for themselves, they destroyed the Avvim, and directly from those Caphtorim Israel conquered the land."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:20:17.273172487Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}